# Har task: deep dive → best logic → optimized, reusable, 100% secure

**User ka hard instruction:** Koi bhi task mile, seedha code likhna shuru mat karo.

## 1. Pehle deep dive
- Affected route → controller → repository/service → model → Blade/JS → tests poora padho
- Same feature ka existing pattern / helper / component dhoondo (`PROJECT_STANDARDS.md` §6g, repositories, services, `app/Support`)
- Side effects check karo: doosre pages, mails, PDFs, exports, AJAX, production (Hostinger) behaviour
- Requirement mein ambiguity ho to assume mat karo — poochho

## 2. Best logic
- Sabse simple + correct solution; edge cases (null, empty, duplicates, permissions, large data) handle karo
- Root cause fix karo, symptom patch nahi

## 3. Optimized
- N+1 avoid: eager load (`with()`), sirf zaroori columns, indexed columns par filter
- Loops mein query mat chalao; bulk operations / `whereIn` use karo
- Heavy kaam dobara na ho (cache / reuse already loaded data)

## 4. Reusable
- Duplicate code mat likho — shared service / repository method / Blade component / JS helper banao ya reuse karo
- Repository pattern follow karo; controller patla rakho

## 5. 100% secure
- Har input validate (`$request->validate`, `mimes`, `max`); mass assignment sirf `validated()` / `only()`
- Authorization: route middleware (`billing`, `accounts.readonly`, roles) + record ownership check
- SQL: query builder / bindings — raw string concat kabhi nahi
- XSS: Blade `{{ }}`, PDF/HTML mein `e()`; JS mein user data escape
- Files: `PrivateDisk`, path traversal se bachao, mime/size validate
- Secrets (`.env`, passwords, tokens) kabhi log/commit/output mat karo
- CSRF, rate limiting jahan applicable

## 6. Done tabhi
- Tests (`composer test`) + localhost smoke (desktop + mobile) + regression test for the change
- Summary mein batao: kya kiya, kyun yeh logic best hai, security/performance considerations
